; ted-mouseinit-allocmem (#367): mouseinit copies the pointer images
; into 152 bytes of chip memory without testing the AllocMem.  TED alone
; under inject: the first AllocMem of 152 bytes of chip memory fails.
; Correct (the fix of the issue: allocfailed): TED ends with a return
; code other than 0 (#357); the original copies the images to address 0
; on (exception vectors, ExecBase) and the system crashes (the session
; hangs).
; @fixed #367
; @source none
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts allocfail=152-152/chip/1 blitz2:ted
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect nostdout "inject: rc=0"
timeout 20
wait exit
